  (text "Notes\nU28: VSEL to GND2 = 3.3 V out (140 mA)\nR165: EN/FLT high (VIO level) enables the DC/DC; reads low on a fault\nU30: pinout checked (SBAS660, 31 Oct). Internal 4.096 MHz clock (CLK to DGND), START low (conversions by command), DOUT/DRDY on one pin\nC145: REFOUT to REFCOM\nR167: RTD reference resistor, 10 ppm/K\nC147: CHECK AINCOM and the TC bias against the io-node schematic\nC148: differential filter\nR168: open-TC bias\nR174: RTD return to the reference resistor\nJ19: T1 +/-, T2 +/-, RTD return\nJ20: T3 +/-, T4 +/-, RTD return\nJ21: T5 +/-, T6 +/-, RTD return\nU31: VSEL to VISOOUT = 5 V out (110 mA)\nR177: EN/FLT high (VIO level) enables the DC/DC; reads low on a fault\nU33: loop power 6 x 22 mA + level + mass-flow supply, about 4 W\nU34: internal oscillator and 2.5 V reference. VIN0/1: 4-20 mA ch 5/6 on shunts; VIN2 level; VIN3 mass flow; VIN4 10 V monitor; VIN5 5 V monitor. Pinout checked (31 Oct); CHECK the exposed pad size against the CP-40 drawing\nR179: 4-20 mA shunt -> 1-5 V; takes the 30 mA limit for ever (0.23 W)\nR180: 4-20 mA shunt -> 1-5 V; takes the 30 mA limit for ever (0.23 W)\nF16: loop current limit; shorted loop = 0.7 W: copper on the cathode. CHECK the 30 mA option, its 2.5 V headroom and the AD4112 IIN abs max\nJ22: per channel: 24 V loop, IN, 0 V (2-wire or 4-wire transmitters)\nJ23: per channel: 24 V loop, IN, 0 V (2-wire or 4-wire transmitters)\nJ24: per channel: 24 V loop, IN, 0 V (2-wire or 4-wire transmitters)\nU35: level sensor 5 V, internal current limit\nR181: defined level when unplugged\nU36: 13 V pre-regulator, about 0.5 W: copper on the VO pins\nR183: 1.25 x (1 + 2260/240) = 13.0 V\nU38: SET driven by the REF5010 (no RSET). CHECK PGFB tie when PG is unused\nR184: about 50 mA current limit"
    (at 15.24 523.24 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left top))
    (uuid fb724f74-9ae1-51ea-8c7f-21b116fcd1e8)
  )
  (text "\nR185: 10 V monitor for ratiometric correction\nD49: clamps +5V_LVL\nD50: clamps +10V_FLOW (12.2 V min breakdown)\nJ25: level (DFRobot SEN0205): 5 V, SIG, 0 V; mass flow (AWM5104VN): +10 V, OUT, 0 V\nU40: NOT FITTED.\nC301: NOT FITTED.\nU39: NOT FITTED. VSEL to VISOOUT = 5 V out (DVDD)\nR301: NOT FITTED. EN/FLT high (VIO level) enables the DC/DC; reads low on a fault\nC302: NOT FITTED.\nC303: NOT FITTED.\nC304: NOT FITTED.\nC305: NOT FITTED.\nC306: NOT FITTED.\nU41: NOT FITTED. AVCC for the four boost converters\nC307: NOT FITTED.\nC308: NOT FITTED.\nC309: NOT FITTED.\nL4: NOT FITTED. boost inductor, as the datasheet test circuit\nD51: NOT FITTED.\nC310: NOT FITTED.\nC311: NOT FITTED.\nC312: NOT FITTED. COMPDCDC\nD55: NOT FITTED. output clamp. CHECK what IOUT survives when 24 V is wired onto it\nC313: NOT FITTED.\nL5: NOT FITTED.\nD52: NOT FITTED.\nC314: NOT FITTED.\nC315: NOT FITTED."
    (at 284.48 523.24 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left top))
    (uuid c6b15fa1-76dd-5328-9cec-98726f869f1d)
  )
  (text "\nC316: NOT FITTED.\nD56: NOT FITTED.\nC317: NOT FITTED.\nL6: NOT FITTED.\nD53: NOT FITTED.\nC318: NOT FITTED.\nC319: NOT FITTED.\nC320: NOT FITTED.\nD57: NOT FITTED.\nC321: NOT FITTED.\nL7: NOT FITTED.\nD54: NOT FITTED.\nC322: NOT FITTED.\nC323: NOT FITTED.\nC324: NOT FITTED.\nD58: NOT FITTED.\nC325: NOT FITTED.\nU42: NOT FITTED. 4 x 4-20 mA, short and open-loop detect. Pin numbers from Table 5 (31 Oct). VOUT/+VSENSE/COMPLV/CHART/RSET unconnected for current-only use: CHECK the datasheet's unused-pin advice\nC326: NOT FITTED.\nC327: NOT FITTED.\nC328: NOT FITTED.\nC329: NOT FITTED. REFOUT to REFIN, 100n to REFGND\nR302: NOT FITTED.\nR303: NOT FITTED.\nR304: NOT FITTED.\nJ26: NOT FITTED. 4-20 mA out: OUTn+, 0 V per channel (active, board powers the loop)"
    (at 556.26 523.24 0)
